      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Last time I checked, VRChat's Image and String loader have a redirect limit of ZERO, as in no redirects at all for security reasons. \n\nAs a world creator I think you SHOULD tell players what to do. You could take in the link, and then present a full watch link as a text box that they can copy out of.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-09T14:06:28.126Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Requesting `https://youtu.be/*videoID*` to StringLoader results in error, saying `Redirect limit exceeded`, where the redirection happens only once (HTTP 303, towards `https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=*videoID*&feature=youtu.be`). \n\nThe reason why this needs to be fixed is to allow Udon to gather content information before feeding the URL to the player. For example, when player loads an URL to the video player, Udon can first look up its web content via StringLoader, parse title/creator/duration/more infos from the result, and show that to the user to confirm that the content the user is trying to load is correct.\n\nAs of 2026/06, dynamic URL creation is still unavailable, that means the dynamic construction of redirection-free URL (Ex: from `youtu.be/*ID*`, parse ID -> reconstruct URL to `youtube.com/watch?v=*ID*`) is impossible, as well.\n\nI (as world creator) cannot request players to \"Please use youtube.com/watch?v= instead of youtu.be!\" just to circumvent this redirection.\n\nFor trusted URLs, allowing 2 or 3 redirections, and untrusted URLs (Allow Untrusted URLs option checked), allowing 1 redirections could massively help for shortened URL redirection.\n\nAlso adding a second layer of security, blocking the request if the redirected URL is not in trusted URL, could also help preventing redirection vulnerability.",
